---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Our Work" description="Research, documentation, knowledge-sharing, partnerships and cultural initiatives that advance the preservation of Agìkūyū heritage.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <img class="hero-img" src="/images/eleven.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="700" />
    <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">Our Work</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Preserving Heritage. Creating Knowledge. <em>Building Connections.</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap tight">
    <div class="prose narrow reveal" style="text-align:center;">
      <p>
        Our Work brings together the research, documentation, knowledge-sharing, partnerships and cultural initiatives
        through which Agìkūyū Women and Men advances its mission.
      </p>
      <p>
        While our Programmes focus on specific groups and learning or cultural activities, Our Work reflects the wider
        work we undertake to document, preserve, develop and share knowledge about Agìkūyū heritage and African cultural thought.
      </p>
    </div>
    <nav class="chip-row reveal" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#research">Research, Knowledge &amp; Publications</a>
      <a href="#heritage">Heritage, Documentation &amp; Partnerships</a>
      <a href="#cultural-projects">Cultural Projects &amp; Knowledge Exchange</a>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <!-- 1. Research, Knowledge & Publications -->
  <section class="section-wrap tight work-section" id="research">
    <div class="row reveal">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="eyebrow">01</div>
        <h2 class="row-title">Research, Knowledge <em>&amp; Publications</em></h2>
        <p>
          Our Research, Knowledge &amp; Publications work provides a space for generating, documenting and sharing knowledge
          emerging from our engagement with Agìkūyū culture, history, language, traditions, indigenous knowledge and African cultural thought.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are interested in research that takes African knowledge systems seriously and creates opportunities for cultural
          knowledge to be documented, examined, preserved and made accessible to Agìkūyū communities and wider audiences.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/eleven.jpg" alt="Archival photograph" width="700" height="520" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <div class="sub-block reveal">
      <h3 class="sub-title">Research Consultancy &amp; Academic Support</h3>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We provide research consultancy and academic support to Master's, Doctorate (PhD) and Postdoctoral students,
          as well as other researchers undertaking research related to Agìkūyū culture and history.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our areas of support may include Agìkūyū history and heritage, Gìkūyū language and oral literature, indigenous
          knowledge systems, religion and spirituality, rituals and cultural practices, gender and community life,
          traditional knowledge and memory, African cultural thought, heritage preservation, and contemporary
          transformations of African traditions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Support may include research topic development, contextual and background research, cultural and historical
          perspectives, research guidance, documentation approaches, interpretation of cultural materials, and, where
          appropriate, connections with relevant knowledge holders and cultural resources.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through this work, we seek to encourage research that is culturally informed, respectful of community knowledge
          and attentive to the richness and diversity of Agìkūyū experiences and histories.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/contact?topic=research-consultancy" class="btn-ghost">Enquire About Research Consultancy</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sub-block reveal">
      <h3 class="sub-title">Publications &amp; Knowledge Sharing</h3>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Our publications library features articles, research papers, essays, educational materials and other original
          publications emerging from our research and engagement with Agìkūyū heritage and African cultural knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Selected publications may be available as paid articles, allowing readers to purchase individual pieces through
          the website using M-Pesa or Visa and access the full publication after payment.
        </p>
        <p>
          This model helps make research and cultural knowledge more accessible while creating a sustainable way of
          supporting continued research, documentation and publication.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/contact?topic=publications" class="btn-ghost">Ask About Publications</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Heritage, Documentation & Partnerships -->
  <section class="section-wrap tight work-section tinted" id="heritage">
    <div class="row reversed reveal">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="eyebrow">02</div>
        <h2 class="row-title">Heritage, Documentation <em>&amp; Partnerships</em></h2>
        <p>
          We document and engage with aspects of Agìkūyū heritage that are at risk of being forgotten or becoming
          inaccessible to future generations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our documentation work includes language, oral traditions, stories, songs, indigenous knowledge, historical
          memory, cultural practices and community knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          We recognize that heritage is not only found in written records. It is also carried through people, families,
          communities, memories, language, practices and intergenerational knowledge. Our work therefore seeks to support
          the careful documentation and transmission of knowledge in ways that respect its cultural context.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/thirteen.jpg" alt="Archival photograph of three elders" width="700" height="520" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <div class="sub-block reveal">
      <h3 class="sub-title">Partnerships &amp; Collaboration</h3>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We collaborate with individuals, researchers, cultural organizations, educational and research institutions,
          community members and other partners whose work contributes to the preservation, documentation and
          transmission of African cultural heritage and knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through these partnerships, we create opportunities for knowledge exchange, collaborative research, cultural
          documentation, educational initiatives and other forms of engagement with Agìkūyū and African heritage.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/partner" class="btn-ghost">Partner With Us</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Cultural Projects & Knowledge Exchange -->
  <section class="section-wrap tight work-section" id="cultural-projects">
    <div class="row reveal">
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="eyebrow">03</div>
        <h2 class="row-title">Cultural Projects <em>&amp; Knowledge Exchange</em></h2>
        <p>
          We develop and support cultural projects that create meaningful opportunities for people to engage with heritage,
          knowledge, language and identity.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our projects may bring together women, men, young people, children, elders, families and communities around
          particular aspects of Agìkūyū heritage and cultural knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          These initiatives may include oral history projects, cultural documentation, language and heritage initiatives,
          educational resources, community-based projects, exhibitions, conversations, storytelling, creative projects
          and other forms of cultural engagement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/ten.jpg" alt="Women in traditional dress singing together" width="700" height="520" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <div class="sub-block reveal">
      <h3 class="sub-title">Across Generations</h3>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We are particularly interested in creating spaces where knowledge can move across generations and between
          communities — from elders to younger people, through families, and between different holders and expressions
          of cultural knowledge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Through our cultural projects, we seek not only to preserve the past but also to create opportunities for
          communities to reconnect with, reflect on and carry their heritage forward.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/contact?topic=cultural-programme" class="btn-ghost">Ask About Cultural Programmes</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
